{
  "cdmVersionRange": ">=5.0.0",
  "_README": [
    "Anemia at the Iannuzzi 2020 threshold: haemoglobin < 10 g/dL (2 points).",
    "",
    "TWO criteria, one per unit. query_anemia_covariate_counts() normalises g/L",
    "to g/dL with `CASE WHEN value_as_number > 25 THEN value/10`; circe has no",
    "arithmetic, so the equivalent is an explicit second criterion at < 100 g/L.",
    "Omitting it would silently drop any site reporting haemoglobin in g/L.",
    "",
    "SEPARATE from cohort 9100009 (the sVQI-FS sex-specific threshold) on",
    "purpose. In pad-amp-nhd-val both scores shared the covariate_id \"anemia\"",
    "and the threshold was chosen by testing whether the covariate FILE PATH",
    "contained the substring \"vqifs\" - a test that also matched an output",
    "folder. Two distinctly-named cohorts make that class of bug impossible.",
    "PrimaryCriteriaLimit / QualifiedLimit / ExpressionLimit are all \"All\" and EndStrategy is StartDate+0, unlike the [DVI] VA-FI cohorts (1797948-1797977) which are \"First\". A first-ever-only cohort cannot answer a lookback-window question."
  ],
